  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Henry Avery was the elusive pirate king who vanished without a trace after
    pulling off one of the greatest heists in history. A former naval officer turned
    outlaw, Avery led a mutiny in 1694 and took command of the Fancy, transforming
    it into one of the fastest and deadliest ships of the era. His crowning achievement?
    The audacious capture of the Mughal treasure ship Ganj-i-Sawai in 1695\u2014one
    of the richest hauls in pirate history, loaded with gold, silver, and jewels. 
    \r\n\r\nUnlike most pirates who met the noose, Avery disappeared into legend,
    his fortune and final fate unknown. Some say he lived out his days as a king
    in Madagascar, others claim he died penniless in hiding. Either way, his legacy
    endures as the man who got away\u2014the pirate who truly vanished into myth.
    \r\n\r\n "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
